<%#
  Shared export-control deny shell (used by the SMP-1852 attestation deny page). Rendered as a LAYOUT: the
  caller passes the heading + retry affordance and yields the denial body.

  Non-bypassable by design — there is NO "continue anyway". The only affordances are to retry (the caller's
  path) or to sign out. The controller renders this with HTTP 403.

  Locals:
    heading     — the <h1> text
    retry_path  — where the primary "try again" link goes
    retry_label — the primary link's label

  NOTE (follow-up): device_location_attestations/denied.html.erb is the same shape and could adopt this
  shell in a one-line change once that deferred (ships-dark) route is picked up. Left untouched here so a
  restyle does not alter a deferred page's rendering.
%>
<%= render "export_control/styles" %>
<main class="ec-page">
  <div class="ec-card ec-card--denied">
    <h1 class="ec-h1 ec-h1--denied"><%= heading %></h1>
    <%# role="alert" so a screen reader announces the block on load — these pages cannot be navigated past. %>
    <div class="ec-body" role="alert">
      <%= yield %>
    </div>
    <div class="ec-actions ec-actions--center">
      <%= link_to retry_label, retry_path, class: "ec-btn ec-btn--primary" %>
      <%# Sign out uses the existing auth0 logout path. %>
      <%= link_to "Sign out", auth0_logout_path, class: "ec-btn ec-btn--secondary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
